Spark is a top-level project of the Apache Software Foundation, designed to be used with a range of programming languages and on a variety of architectures. Spark is quickly becoming Spark training in bay area <http://www.bigdatatrunk.com/> the figure out/calculate engine of choice for big data. Spark programs are more well-said with a small number of words and often run 10-100 times faster than Hadoop MapReduce jobs. Spark training in bay area  is designed both batch processing (almost the same to MapReduce) and new workloads like streaming, interactive questions, and machine learning.    People who are looking for big data class room training in bay area , BigData trunk will provide Spark  with experienced faculty in union city.

